lama.cpp + Vulkan (AMD 780M) – Working Setup Guide
1. Install required Vulkan tools

You need the system Vulkan SDK tools (for glslc):

sudo apt install -y libvulkan-dev mesa-vulkan-drivers mesa-vulkan-drivers:i386 shaderc-tools


Confirm glslc exists:

which glslc

2. Clone llama.cpp and create a clean build folder
cd ~/dev
git clone https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp.git
cd llama.cpp
rm -rf build
mkdir build && cd build


A clean build is required any time Vulkan wasn't detected earlier.

3. Configure CMake with Vulkan enabled
cmake .. -DGGML_VULKAN=ON


You must see:

-- Including Vulkan backend
-- Vulkan found


If it doesn't show that → stop and fix before building.

4. Build llama.cpp with Vulkan backend
cmake --build . -j$(nproc)

5. Fix permissions for GPU access

Your user must belong to these groups:

sudo usermod -aG render $USER
sudo usermod -aG video $USER


Log out completely or reboot.

Confirm:

groups


Should show:

video render

6. Test Vulkan visibility (normal user)
vulkaninfo | grep -i radeon


You should NOT run this with sudo.

Expected:

deviceName = AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV PHOENIX)

7. Run llama.cpp with GPU offloading

Example:

/home/mikeathan/dev/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-cli \
  --model ~/dev/models/qwen2.5-3b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf \
  --gpu-layers 50 \
  --prompt "hi"


Expected message:

ggml_vulkan: Found 1 Vulkan devices:
ggml_vulkan: using AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV PHOENIX)